Since ABCD is divisible by 3, A + B + C + D is divisible by 3 and hence BDAC is also divisible by 3. Other arrangements printed in the answer are:
ABDC, ACBD, ACDB, ADCB, ADBC;
BDCA, BCDA, BCAD, BACD, BADC;
CABD, CADB, CBDA, CBAD, CDAB, CDBA;
DABC, DACB, DCBA, DCAB, DBAC, DBCA.
